{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016vb3rsdyYcA3Ar2pcZuHBx","type":"tool_result","content":"81:| §4 | Changing the Fleet Under Way | **rolling-update mechanics** — `maxSurge`, `maxUnavailable`, Recreate; pause/resume (strategy *vocabulary* deferred to Ch 15 §2) |\n82-| §5 | Every Rollout Is a Revision | revisions; rollout history; **`kubectl rollout undo`** (distinct from Helm rollback — see Ch 14 §3) |\n83-| §6 | When Pods Are Not Interchangeable | StatefulSet; stable ordinal identity; why identity, not disk-writing, is the distinction. **The book's one deliberate forward reference** — PV pairing completed at Ch 11 §6 |\n84-| §7 | One Per Node, and Work That Ends | DaemonSet; Job; CronJob; completion and parallelism semantics |\n--\n214:*Decay-risk note (B3): Helm has thin downstream presence. The two mandatory anchors are Ch 15 §4 (charts as an Argo CD manifest source) and Ch 17 §4 (CRDs shipped as chart content). Neither may be dropped.*\n215-\n216----\n217-\n218:## Ch 15 — The Chart Is the Truth  [PLANNED]\n219-\n220-| § | Title | Owns |\n221-|---|---|---|\n--\n230:*Published pointer honored: `Ch 15 §4 — the delivery agent's identity`. This pins Argo CD to §4, which pushed the four OpenGitOps principles up into §3 alongside push-vs-pull. That merge is defensible — the principles are the pull model's definition — but it means `ch15-fig05-opengitops-four-principles` renders inside §3, not in a section of its own.*\n231-\n232----\n233-\n--\n354:| Ch 15 §4 — the delivery agent's identity | Argo CD pinned to §4, pushing the OpenGitOps principles up into §3 |\n355-| Ch 16 §1, §2 | init-container debugging ahead of exec/ephemeral containers |\n356-| Ch 17 §1, §2, §4 | definition, governance+maturity, and the collected interfaces at fixed slots |\n357-| Ch 18 §1, §3 | the observability/health distinction at §1; utilization-vs-requests at §3 |\n--\n368:| The control loop | Ch 3 §6 | Ch 6 §2, Ch 11 §2, Ch 15 §7, Ch 17 §4 |\n369-| Namespaced vs cluster-scoped | Ch 4 §3 | Ch 8 §3, Ch 12 §3 |\n370-| Labels and selectors | Ch 4 §5 | Ch 6 §3, Ch 7 §3, Ch 9 §4, Ch 10 §6, Ch 16 §4 |\n371-| Requests, limits, QoS | Ch 5 §8 | Ch 7 §2, Ch 13 §4, Ch 17 §7, Ch 18 §3 |\n372:| ServiceAccount identity | Ch 5 §6 (object) / Ch 12 §2 (as RBAC subject) | Ch 15 §4 |\n373:| Rolling-update mechanics | Ch 6 §4 | Ch 15 §2 owns the strategy *vocabulary* only |\n374-| Rollback | Ch 6 §5 (`kubectl rollout undo`) | Ch 14 §3 owns Helm rollback and the name collision |\n375-| StatefulSet | Ch 6 §6 (identity) / Ch 11 §6 (storage pairing) | Ch 16 §6 |\n376-| Version skew | Ch 8 §6 | Ch 13 §6, Ch 17 §8 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b05eb31d-1c28-48b6-bc35-59f5a9d9b150","uuid":"49d13067-b566-4007-ab55-caec1f1dfc14","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:18:10.346Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"81:| §4 | Changing the Fleet Under Way | **rolling-update mechanics** — `maxSurge`, `maxUnavailable`, Recreate; pause/resume (strategy *vocabulary* deferred to Ch 15 §2) |\n82-| §5 | Every Rollout Is a Revision | revisions; rollout history; **`kubectl rollout undo`** (distinct from Helm rollback — see Ch 14 §3) |\n83-| §6 | When Pods Are Not Interchangeable | StatefulSet; stable ordinal identity; why identity, not disk-writing, is the distinction. **The book's one deliberate forward reference** — PV pairing completed at Ch 11 §6 |\n84-| §7 | One Per Node, and Work That Ends | DaemonSet; Job; CronJob; completion and parallelism semantics |\n--\n214:*Decay-risk note (B3): Helm has thin downstream presence. The two mandatory anchors are Ch 15 §4 (charts as an Argo CD manifest source) and Ch 17 §4 (CRDs shipped as chart content). Neither may be dropped.*\n215-\n216----\n217-\n218:## Ch 15 — The Chart Is the Truth  [PLANNED]\n219-\n220-| § | Title | Owns |\n221-|---|---|---|\n--\n230:*Published pointer honored: `Ch 15 §4 — the delivery agent's identity`. This pins Argo CD to §4, which pushed the