{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MJaofJ3gfsDThpiehfmbAK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://fluxcd.io/flux/concepts/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T06:15:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Flux project (CNCF graduated)\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D3.1\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"flux\", \"flux-controller-set\", \"flux-bootstrap\", \"continuously-reconciled-principle\", \"drift-detection\", \"manifest-source\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Flux — Core concepts (2026-08-31 capture)\n9\t\n10\t## GitOps Toolkit\n11\t\"In Flux, GitOps Toolkit refers to a collection of specialized tools, Flux Controllers, composable APIs, and reusable Go packages available under the fluxcd GitHub organization.\"\n12\t\n13\t## Sources\n14\t\"A Source defines the origin of a repository containing the desired state of the system and the requirements to obtain it (e.g. credentials, version selectors).\"\n15\t\n16\t## Reconciliation\n17\t\"Reconciliation refers to ensuring that a given state (e.g. application running in the cluster, infrastructure) matches a desired state declaratively defined somewhere (e.g. a Git repository).\"\n18\t\n19\t\"The reconciliation runs every five minutes by default, but this can be changed with `.spec.interval`.\"\n20\t\n21\t\"If you make any changes to the cluster using `kubectl edit/patch/delete`, they will be promptly reverted.\"\n22\t\n23\t## Bootstrap\n24\t\"The process of installing the Flux components in a GitOps manner is called a bootstrap. The manifests are applied to the cluster, a `GitRepository` and `Kustomization` are created for the Flux components, then the manifests are pushed to an existing Git repository (or a new one is created).\"\n25\t\n26\tCAPTURE NOTE: the GitOps Toolkit definition differs from the 2026-08-23 capture,\n27\twhich read \"Flux is a GitOps Toolkit: a set of composable APIs and specialized\n28\ttools.\" Both captures are retained. Cite this one for the current wording.\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b05eb31d-1c28-48b6-bc35-59f5a9d9b150","uuid":"d1126ee8-f654-4f7c-953c-21aea2100294","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:19:51.741Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/flux-concepts-2026-08-31.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://fluxcd.io/flux/concepts/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T06:15:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Flux project (CNCF graduated)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D3.1\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"flux\", \"flux-controller-set\", \"flux-bootstrap\", \"continuously-reconciled-principle\", \"drift-detection\", \"manifest-source\"]\n---\n# Flux — Core concepts (2026-08-31 capture)\n\n## GitOps Toolkit\n\"In Flux, GitOps Toolkit refers to a collection of specialized tools, Flux Controllers, composable APIs, and reusable Go packages available under the fluxcd GitHub organization.\"\n\n## Sources\n\"A Source defines the origin of a repository containing the desired state of the system and the requirements to obtain it (e.g. credentials, version selectors).\"\n\n## Reconciliation\n\"Reconciliation refers to ensuring that a given state (e.g. application running in the cluster, infrastructure) matches a desired state declaratively defined somewhere (e.g. a Git repository).\"\n\n\"The reconciliation runs every five minutes by default, but this can be changed with `.spec.interval`.\"\n\n\"If you make any changes to the cluster using `kubectl edit/patch/delete`, they will be promptly reverted.\"\n\n## Bootstrap\n\"The process of installing the Flux components in a GitOps manner is called a bootstrap. The manifests are applied to the cluster, a `GitRepository` and `Kustomization` are created for the Flux components, then the manifests are pushed to an existing Git repository (or a new one is created).\"\n\nCAPTURE NOTE: the GitOps Toolkit definition differs from the 2026-08-23 capture,\nwhich read \"Flux is a GitOps Toolkit: a set of composable APIs and specialized\ntools.\" Both captures are retained. Cite this one for the current wording.\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}}}
