{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EqhUwzAtQqtmkvJMw5AWPf","type":"tool_result","content":"306:## ⚪ §1 — The Resource That Holds the Intent\n376:## ⚪ §2 — A Loop You Can Watch Working\n435:## 🔵 §3 — How a Controller Knows Its Own\n445:> **Before reading on:** the labels in the Pod template do not match the selector. The controller creates a Pod from the template, and then cannot see it. Work out what happens next before you read the answer. It takes about ten seconds and the answer is worth deriving yourself.\n555:## 🔵 §4 — Changing the Fleet Under Way\n669:## 🔵 §5 — Every Rollout Is a Revision\n798:## 🔵 §6 — When Pods Are Not Interchangeable\n878:## ⚪ §7 — One Per Node, and Work That Ends\n969:## 🟡 §8 — The Control Loop, Extended\n1101:## ☀️ §9 — Nobody Sails One Pod\n1147:When you meet that, it will look like a new idea for about ten seconds.\n1465:And one thing that is not a bullet point: you have seen the control loop twice now, at two altitudes, and recognized it the second time. Hold onto that recognition. You are going to need it once more, and the third time is the one that matters."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b05eb31d-1c28-48b6-bc35-59f5a9d9b150","uuid":"2fabd7e2-ff94-497f-8fa6-68bb1596b56a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:20:30.766Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"306:## ⚪ §1 — The Resource That Holds the Intent\n376:## ⚪ §2 — A Loop You Can Watch Working\n435:## 🔵 §3 — How a Controller Knows Its Own\n445:> **Before reading on:** the labels in the Pod template do not match the selector. The controller creates a Pod from the template, and then cannot see it. Work out what happens next before you read the answer. It takes about ten seconds and the answer is worth deriving yourself.\n555:## 🔵 §4 — Changing the Fleet Under Way\n669:## 🔵 §5 — Every Rollout Is a Revision\n798:## 🔵 §6 — When Pods Are Not Interchangeable\n878:## ⚪ §7 — One Per Node, and Work That Ends\n969:## 🟡 §8 — The Control Loop, Extended\n1101:## ☀️ §9 — Nobody Sails One Pod\n1147:When you meet that, it will look like a new idea for about ten seconds.\n1465:And one thing that is not a bullet point: you have seen the control loop twice now, at two altitudes, and recognized it the second time. Hold onto that recognition. You are going to need it once more, and the third time is the one that matters.","numLines":12,"totalLines":12}}
